// SourceCrate Browser UI - API Configuration
//
// ⚠️ IMPORTANT: This file should ONLY exist in local development!
//              It is auto-generated by scripts/local-manager.sh
//              Do NOT commit this file to git (it's in .gitignore)
//
// === LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ===
// The local-manager.sh script auto-generates this file.
// You can also manually create it for custom local setups:
//   1. Copy: cp config.js.example config.js
//   2. Uncomment and set your local API URL below
//
// For standard local development, the UI auto-detects:
//   - UI on port 3000 → API on port 9000
//   - UI on port 3001 → API on port 9000 (devcontainer)
//   - Default fallback → http://localhost:9000

// === PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT ===
// ✅ DO NOT create config.js in production!
//
// The UI automatically detects production environments:
// - When no port (e.g., https://sourcecrate.fly.dev)
// - When standard HTTP(S) ports (80/443)
// → Uses same-origin: window.location.protocol + window.location.hostname
//
// This works automatically for:
// ✅ Fly.io deployments (with [[statics]] serving UI + API on same domain)
// ✅ Any deployment serving UI and API on the same origin
//
// ❌ ONLY create config.js if deploying UI and API on DIFFERENT domains:

// Separate deployment example (uncomment if needed):
// window.SOURCECRATE_API_URL = 'https://api.example.com';

// === LOCAL DEVELOPMENT MANUAL OVERRIDE ===
// Uncomment to force a specific local port (usually not needed):
// window.SOURCECRATE_API_URL = 'http://localhost:9000';
